--- !u!1001 &5428359423457015080
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 5140518586754131107}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 1881534070420041712, guid: b57e20b9f2df91e42a4c142e53793094, type: 3}
      propertyPath: day
      value: 8
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1881534070420041712, guid: b57e20b9f2df91e42a4c142e53793094, type: 3}
      propertyPath: desc
      value: "<size=115%><b>[San Francisco, CA \u2013 May 27, 2025]</b></size> \u2014
        SnapGram, a leading social media platform connecting over <b>1.2 billion
        users worldwide</b>, acknowledges recent media reports concerning the handling
        of user data by certain third-party partners. While the reports have sparked
        conversation and concern, SnapGram remains steadfast in its commitment to
        maintaining a <b>safe, engaging, and personalized experience</b> for all
        users.\n\nRecent investigative journalism has drawn attention to data-sharing
        practices that involved select <b>marketing affiliates</b> and <b>analytics
        providers</b>. These arrangements, common across the tech industry, were
        designed to enhance user experiences through better-targeted features and
        relevant content. While SnapGram recognizes that the reporting has raised
        valid questions, it is important to clarify that any data shared was done
        so under <i>broadly accepted operational frameworks</i>.\n\nSnapGram has
        always prioritized <b>innovation</b> and <b>user-centric design</b>. Our
        privacy policy, available publicly and agreed to by all users upon sign-up,
        outlines the scope of data use in accordance with applicable laws. We understand
        that, in hindsight, some users may have expected greater specificity. We
        regret any confusion that may have arisen and are reviewing our communications
        to ensure <b>clearer language</b> in the future.\n\n<i>\u201CWe understand
        the public\u2019s desire for increased transparency,\u201D</i> said <b>Emery
        Kaczmarek Johnson</b>, VP of Policy and Trust at SnapGram. <i>\u201CWhile
        we do not agree with some of the conclusions being drawn, we are actively
        assessing our internal protocols and third-party relationships. We want to
        reassure users that their trust is critical to us.\u201D</i>\n\nSnapGram
        stresses that at no point was any data <b>\u201Csold\u201D</b> in the traditional
        sense. Rather, selected <b>metadata</b> was utilized within a network of
        service agreements intended to support <b>app functionality</b> and <b>user
        engagement</b>. No <b>personally identifiable financial data</b>, <b>direct
        messages</b>, or <b>private content</b> was disclosed to outside vendors.\n\nThe
        company has engaged an <b>independent privacy auditor</b> to evaluate past
        processes and offer recommendations for future enhancements. This initiative
        reinforces SnapGram\u2019s long-standing belief in evolving its practices
        to meet the shifting expectations of a global community.\n\nSnapGram is launching
        a redesigned <b><color=#B4114B>\u201CPrivacy Center\u201D</color></b> within
        the app that provides users with a simplified overview of how their data
        is used, with <b>new controls</b> rolling out over the next two months. These
        changes reflect SnapGram\u2019s <b>proactive posture</b>, rather than any
        admission of wrongdoing.\n\n<i>\u201CWe see this moment as a chance to listen,
        reflect, and improve,\u201D</i> said Kaczmarek Johnson. <i>\u201CWe encourage
        all users to explore the new Privacy Center when it becomes available and
        to reach out with feedback.\u201D</i>\n\n<b>For media inquiries, please contact:</b> 
        \n<color=#3366CC>press@snapgram.com</color>\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1881534070420041712, guid: b57e20b9f2df91e42a4c142e53793094, type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Press Release
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1881534070420041712, guid: b57e20b9f2df91e42a4c142e53793094, type: 3}
      propertyPath: subtitle
      value: SnapGram Addresses Recent User Data Concerns, Reaffirming Our Commitment
        to Transparency
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 2068048972840628376, guid: b57e20b9f2df91e42a4c142e53793094, type: 3}
